{
  "id": "V02",
  "title": "Two unequal walls + self-weight",
  "intent": "Capacity distribution between two solid walls of different length (8 ft and 12 ft) at one story, with each wall carrying only its own self-weight. Proves weight = v_cap × L, share = V × weight / Σ weight, the equal unit shear that follows, and per-wall overturning, holdown and post.",
  "covers": [
    "SDPWS 2021 §4.3.3.4.1 capacity distribution",
    "SDPWS Table 4.3A + footnote 10",
    "ASCE 7-22 §2.4.5 (5), (8)",
    "HDUE selection",
    "G2 horizontal equilibrium"
  ],
  "handCalc": [
    {
      "step": 1,
      "text": "Story shear V = 1.0E = 10 k. Walls SW-1 L = 8 ft, SW-2 L = 12 ft, h = 10 ft (h/b = 1.25 and 0.83, both ≤ 2 → C_hb = 1.0)."
    },
    {
      "step": 2,
      "text": "Nailing trial: with one pattern at both walls v = 0.7 × 10000 / (8 + 12) = 350.00 plf → 4\" o.c. (470 plf)."
    },
    {
      "step": 3,
      "text": "Weights = v_cap × L: SW-1 470 × 8 = 3760 lb, SW-2 470 × 12 = 5640 lb, Σ = 9400 lb."
    },
    {
      "step": 4,
      "text": "Shares: V_1 = 10 × 3760 / 9400 = 4.000 k, V_2 = 10 × 5640 / 9400 = 6.000 k (Σ = 10.00 k)."
    },
    {
      "step": 5,
      "text": "Unit shear: v_1 = 0.7 × 4000.00 / 8 = 350.00 plf, v_2 = 0.7 × 6000.00 / 12 = 350.00 plf → both 4\" o.c., D/C = 350.00 / 470 = 0.745."
    },
    {
      "step": 6,
      "text": "Self-weight: D_1 = 10 × 8 × 10 / 1000 = 0.80 k (R = 0.40 each end); D_2 = 10 × 12 × 10 / 1000 = 1.20 k (R = 0.60)."
    },
    {
      "step": 7,
      "text": "Overturning 1.0E: N_1 = 4.000 × 10 / 8 = 5.000 k; N_2 = 6.000 × 10 / 12 = 5.000 k (equal: same v at both walls)."
    },
    {
      "step": 8,
      "text": "Uplift (0.6 − 0.14S_DS)D + 0.7E: T_1 = 0.7 × 5.000 − 0.46 × 0.40 = 3.316 k → HDUE3; T_2 = 0.7 × 5.000 − 0.46 × 0.60 = 3.224 k → HDUE3."
    },
    {
      "step": 9,
      "text": "Compression (1.0 + 0.14S_DS)D + 0.7E: C_1 = 1.14 × 0.40 + 0.7 × 5.000 = 3.956 k; C_2 = 1.14 × 0.60 + 0.7 × 5.000 = 4.184 k."
    },
    {
      "step": 10,
      "text": "End posts: HDUE3 minimum post (2)2x4; NDS cap at 10 ft = 5.00 k ≥ 4.184 k → (2)2x4 at every end."
    },
    {
      "step": 11,
      "text": "SW-1 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 4.000 / 8 = 500.00 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 20 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0280; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.2500; uplift end T = 5000.00 lb (lateral); Δ_HD = δ_LRFD × T / T_LRFD = 0.178 × 5000.00 / 5306 = 0.1677 (HDUE3); r = 5000.00 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.7619 → Δ_c = 0.0224; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.1677 + 0.0224) / 8 = 0.2376 → δ = 0.5156 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 12,
      "text": "SW-2 (Eq. 4.3-1, → governs): v = 1000 × 6.000 / 12 = 500.00 plf, A = 10.5 in², G_a = 20 k/in → 8vh³/(EAb) = 0.0187; vh/(1000G_a) = 0.2500; uplift end T = 5000.00 lb (lateral); Δ_HD = δ_LRFD × T / T_LRFD = 0.178 × 5000.00 / 5306 = 0.1677 (HDUE3); r = 5000.00 / (10.5 × 625) = 0.7619 → Δ_c = 0.0224; h·Δa/b = 10 × (0.1677 + 0.0224) / 12 = 0.1584 → δ = 0.4271 in."
    },
    {
      "step": 13,
      "text": "Story drift Level 1: δxe = the largest wall δ = SW-1 0.5156 in → δx = Cd·δxe/Ie = 4 × 0.5156 / 1.0 = 2.063 in vs Δa = 0.020 × 10 × 12 = 2.400 in → OK."
    }
  ],
